      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Excess angiotensin II leads to severe vasoconstriction, which drastically increases systemic vascular resistance and forces the volume to rise, causing acute hypertension. This buildup also over-stimulates the adrenal glands to flood the circulatory system with aldosterone, leading to dangerous fluid overload, potassium depletion, and increased strain on the heart. Ultimately, this chronic hyperactivity promotes arterial stiffening and exacerbates conditions like heart failure or kidney damage due to sustained pressure.",
